---
import SectionHandoff from '../SectionHandoff.astro';
// The one thing the page never said out loud: how the prices get IN.
//
// WHY THIS SECTION EXISTS. Every other stop argues the chain (cost it, buy it,
// prep it, pack it, bring the price back). The chain starts from current
// prices, and the page had no slot that said where current prices come from.
// Meanwhile the largest group on /features is "Import & AI intake" (twenty
// items), and src/lib/workflow.ts has carried the best intake copy in the repo
// since it was written, imported by nothing. Competitors lead with this; we
// ship it and say nothing.
//
// TRUTH PASS. Four rows carry this, one per sentence, and nothing here goes
// past them. Two of them were opened FOR this section, because presence in
// features.ts is not ledger backing:
//   RC-38  One queue takes a photo, a PDF, a spreadsheet, a Word document or
//          pasted text. Backs "four doors, one queue". Opened 2026-08-23 off
//          the app's ImportDropzone accept list, not off /features.
//   RC-09  Imported information remains staged until the user reviews and
//          commits it. So every sentence is you-confirm shaped. "Staged until
//          you commit it", never "it reads your invoices".
//   RC-39  What extraction could not read is surfaced verbatim beside what it
//          staged. Backs the quoted-back sentence. Also opened 2026-08-23.
//   RC-26  Purchases enter through posted receiving, invoice import, or manual
//          entry. Manual is named on purpose: the ledger's exclusion list
//          forbids both of the phrases that promise a kitchen never types
//          anything, and keying the awkward invoice in is a supported path
//          here, not a failure. (Those two phrases are deliberately not
//          written out in this comment: the guard scans whole files, comments
//          included, which is the point.)
// Also excluded and deliberately absent: production-certified OCR accuracy,
// and any fully-automatic import or matching promise.
//
// NOT A SECOND TELLING OF OUTCOME FOUR. CustomerOutcomes' "Bring the real
// price back to the next quote" is the receiving-writes-the-purchase loop:
// prices you have already paid. This is the other direction, prices a supplier
// sends you before you buy. Adjacent, not the same promise. If either one is
// ever rewritten toward the other, one of them has to go.
//
// NO SCREENSHOT, DELIBERATELY. public/proof carries the yield crops and
// nothing else, and capturing the diff review needs a staged import batch the
// walkthrough seed does not create. The honest options were a gap or a mock.
// A page whose argument is that the number never lies does not mock a screen.
// If the app repo's @landing test ever produces an import crop, it belongs
// here and the alt text is prospect-facing copy like every other alt in
// src/components/sections.
//
// THE ANCHOR IS UNREFERENCED ON PURPOSE. Nothing enumerates section anchors
// (Hero links #demo and that is the only cross-section href on the page), so
// id="intake" exists for deep links and for parity with its neighbours, not
// for a nav that does not exist.
//
// NO CTA HERE. The primary lives once, at the close. Quiet secondaries are at
// their cap of two already.

// The accept list, in the order RC-38 states it. Photograph, PDF, spreadsheet,
// Word document, pasted text - the Word document rides with the PDF because a
// fifth door reads as a feature list and the queue does not care which it was.
// Considered Composite; not used because four fixed sources converge into one
// static editorial diagram, not a tree of parts with shared behaviour.
const doors = [
	{
		label: 'Photograph it',
		iconPaths: ['M5 8h3l1.5-2h5L16 8h3v10H5z', 'M12 11a3 3 0 1 0 0 6 3 3 0 0 0 0-6z']
	},
	{
		label: 'Drop the PDF or the doc in',
		iconPaths: ['M7 3h7l4 4v14H7z', 'M14 3v5h5', 'M10 12h5', 'M10 16h5']
	},
	{
		label: 'Upload the spreadsheet',
		iconPaths: ['M5 4h14v16H5z', 'M5 9h14', 'M10 9v11', 'M14.5 9v11', 'M5 14h14']
	},
	{
		label: 'Paste the text',
		iconPaths: ['M9 5h6', 'M8 7H6v14h12V7h-2', 'M9 3h6v4H9z', 'M9 12h6', 'M9 16h6']
	}
];
---

<!-- story: docs/stories/homepage-paper-in-visual.story.md -->
<!-- story: docs/stories/homepage-copy-density.story.md -->
<section id="intake" class="container-page border-t border-hairline py-section" aria-labelledby="intake-heading">
	<div class="split-layout intake-layout">
		<div class="intake-copy" data-reveal>
			<p class="eyebrow">Before any of that</p>
			<h2 id="intake-heading" class="mt-4 text-h2 font-semibold">
				Paper in, staged facts out, you confirm.
			</h2>
			<p class="mt-5 text-lede text-ink-soft">
				All of this runs on what your food costs this week, so something has to get the
				price board, the order guide and the invoices in. Four doors, one queue.
			</p>
		</div>

		<figure class="intake-map" data-paper-intake data-reveal>
			<figcaption class="sr-only">
				A photograph, document, spreadsheet or pasted text enters one staging queue. The
				queue lists differences, quotes unclear text and waits for your confirmation.
			</figcaption>

			<div class="source-side">
				<p class="map-label">Four ways in</p>
				<ul role="list" class="source-list">
					{
						doors.map((door) => (
							<li data-intake-source={door.label}>
								<span class="source-icon" aria-hidden="true">
									<svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
										{door.iconPaths.map((path) => <path d={path} />)}
									</svg>
								</span>
								<span>{door.label}</span>
							</li>
						))
					}
				</ul>
			</div>

			<div class="flow-bridge" aria-hidden="true">
				<span></span>
			</div>

			<div class="queue-sheet" data-intake-queue>
				<div class="queue-head">
					<p class="map-label">One review queue</p>
					<span>Nothing written yet</span>
				</div>
				<ul role="list" class="queue-list">
					<li>
						<span class="queue-mark" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
						<div><strong>Differences listed</strong><small>What changed stays visible.</small></div>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="queue-mark" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
						<div><strong>Unclear text quoted</strong><small>The source is shown, not guessed.</small></div>
					</li>
				</ul>
				<div class="confirm-gate" data-intake-confirmation>
					<span>Your gate</span>
					<strong>You confirm</strong>
				</div>
			</div>
		</figure>
	</div>

	<div class="review-copy" data-reveal>
		<!-- CUT 2026-09-09, copy-density pass. This paragraph said, in prose, the three
		     things the queue beside it renders as labels: "Differences listed", "Nothing
		     written yet" with the confirm gate, and "Unclear text quoted / The source is
		     shown, not guessed". The one clause the diagram cannot draw is the one that
		     stayed. BRIEF-copy-density-2026-09-09.md -->
		<p>
			What comes back is a list to look at, not a catalog that changed behind you.
		</p>
		<div class="manual-note">
			<svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
				<path d="M6 3h12v18H6z" />
				<path d="M9 8h6M9 12h6M9 16h3" />
			</svg>
			<p>
				The awkward invoice you would rather key in by hand is still a supported way to do
				it. Reading the paper is the fast part. Saying yes to it is yours.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>

	<SectionHandoff from="intake" />
</section>

<style>
	/* The grid itself is .split-layout in global.css; this names the gap and the
	   one alignment that differs: the queue diagram is centred against its prose,
	   not top-aligned. See the note there on the 27rem track floor. */
	.intake-layout {
		--split-gap: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 5.5rem);
		--split-align: center;
	}

	.intake-copy {
		max-width: 37rem;
	}

	.intake-map {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1.25rem;
		padding: 1.25rem;
		border-block: 1px solid var(--color-ticket-rule);
		background: var(--color-cream);
	}

	.map-label {
		font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace;
		font-size: var(--text-label-sm);
		font-weight: 700;
		line-height: 1.2;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--color-amber-deep);
	}

	.source-list {
		display: grid;
		margin-top: 0.75rem;
	}

	.source-list li {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 2.25rem minmax(0, 1fr);
		gap: 0.75rem;
		align-items: center;
		min-height: 3.25rem;
		padding-block: 0.5rem;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-ticket-rule);
		font-size: var(--text-body-sm);
		font-weight: 600;
	}

	.source-icon {
		display: grid;
		place-items: center;
		width: 2.25rem;
		height: 2.25rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--color-ticket-rule);
		border-radius: 999px;
		background: var(--color-paper);
		color: var(--color-amber-deep);
	}

	.source-icon svg,
	.manual-note svg {
		stroke: currentColor;
		stroke-width: 1.7;
		stroke-linecap: round;
		stroke-linejoin: round;
	}

	.flow-bridge {
		display: grid;
		place-items: center;
		height: 1.5rem;
	}

	.flow-bridge span {
		position: relative;
		display: block;
		width: 1px;
		height: 100%;
		background: var(--color-amber-deep);
	}

	.flow-bridge span::after {
		position: absolute;
		bottom: 0;
		left: -3px;
		width: 7px;
		height: 7px;
		border-right: 1.5px solid var(--color-amber-deep);
		border-bottom: 1.5px solid var(--color-amber-deep);
		content: '';
		transform: rotate(45deg);
	}

	.queue-sheet {
		border: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
		background: var(--color-paper);
		box-shadow: var(--shadow-ticket);
	}

	.queue-head {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.5rem 1rem;
		justify-content: space-between;
		align-items: baseline;
		padding: 1rem;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
	}

	.queue-head > span {
		font-size: var(--text-caption);
		font-weight: 600;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
	}

	.queue-list li {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1.75rem minmax(0, 1fr);
		gap: 0.75rem;
		align-items: start;
		padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
	}

	.queue-mark {
		display: grid;
		place-items: center;
		width: 1.5rem;
		height: 1.5rem;
		border-radius: 999px;
		background: var(--color-softamber);
		font-size: var(--text-micro);
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--color-amber-deep);
	}

	.queue-list strong,
	.queue-list small {
		display: block;
	}

	.queue-list strong {
		font-size: var(--text-body-sm);
	}

	.queue-list small {
		margin-top: 0.2rem;
		font-size: var(--text-caption);
		line-height: 1.4;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
	}

	.confirm-gate {
		display: flex;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		justify-content: space-between;
		align-items: center;
		padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
		background: var(--color-softgreen);
		color: var(--color-green-deep);
	}

	.confirm-gate span {
		font-size: var(--text-caption);
		font-weight: 600;
	}

	.confirm-gate strong {
		font-size: var(--text-body-sm);
	}

	.review-copy {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 30rem), 1fr));
		gap: 1.5rem;
		margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
		padding-top: 1.5rem;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
	}

	.review-copy > p {
		max-width: 43rem;
	}

	.manual-note {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1.5rem minmax(0, 1fr);
		gap: 0.875rem;
		max-width: 36rem;
	}

	.manual-note svg {
		color: var(--color-amber-deep);
	}

	@media (min-width: 48rem) {
		.intake-map {
			grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.9fr) 3rem minmax(0, 1.1fr);
			gap: 0;
			align-items: center;
			padding: 1.5rem;
		}

		.flow-bridge {
			height: auto;
		}

		.flow-bridge span {
			width: 100%;
			height: 1px;
		}

		.flow-bridge span::after {
			top: -3px;
			right: 0;
			bottom: auto;
			left: auto;
			transform: rotate(-45deg);
		}
	}

	@media (min-width: 64rem) {
		.review-copy {
			gap: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 5rem);
		}

		.manual-note {
			max-width: none;
		}
	}
</style>
